Since the SSL on the source domain is the blocker, the quickest fix is to tell WordPress to skip SSL verification when fetching remote images:
Add this to your wp-config.php on the Cloudways site:


phpadd_filter('https_ssl_verify', '__return_false');
add_filter('https_local_ssl_verify', '__return_false');





Or better, add it via functions.php so it doesn't touch wp-config.php:

phpadd_filter('https_ssl_verify', '__return_false');
add_filter('https_local_ssl_verify', '__return_false');




Then try your Elementor import again — it should now be able to fetch images from the Hostinger site without SSL blocking it.

⚠️ Remove this code after you're done importing. Leaving SSL verification disabled permanently is a security risk.

